        "Saguchiya River"
      ],
      "notes_ja": "このハザードマップは、Oi River、Yui River、Saguchiya River の 3 河川が、1000 年に一度起こりうる大規模な大雨により氾濫し堤防が壊れた場合の、浸水被害の危険が高い想定区域と最大浸水深を同時に示している。",
      "source_page": 8,
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 8,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "(22)\r\n(27)\r\n(25) (21)\r\n(26)\r\n(24)\r\nYoshida Town Hall\r\n(18)\r\n(23)\r\n(15)\r\n(14)\r\n(17)\r\n(12)\r\n(10)\r\n(19)\r\n(11)\r\n(16)\r\n(８)\r\n(13)\r\n(3)\r\n(2)\r\n(4)\r\n(7)\r\n(6)\r\n(9) (5)\r\n(1)\r\n(20)\r\nKando Community Center\r\nYoshida-cho Health & Welfare Center-Heartful\r\nSayuri Nursery School\r\nSumire Nusery School\r\nNorth Oasis Park (Oasis Community Center)\r\nKawashiri Community Center\r\nChuo Elementary School\r\nMarch 15,2019\r\nDesignated date Designated precondition of rainfall\r\nTotal rainfall for 18 hours is 772.0mm\r\nTotal rainfall of 729.3mm in 14hours\r\nDesignated precondition of rainfall\r\nMarch 15,2019 Shizuoka \r\nPrefecture\r\nSource Designated date\r\nTotal rainfall for 2\r\ndays is 787mm\r\nDesignated precondition of rainfall\r\nJune 21,2019\r\nDesignated date\r\nShizuoka River \r\nManagement \r\nOi River Flood Inundation Risk Area （Estimated Large Scale)\r\nYoshida Town Hall\r\nYoshida Town Hall\r\nYoshida Town Hall\r\nしていきんきゅうひなんばしょ\r\n指定緊急避難場所\r\nしていひなんじょ\r\n指定避難所\r\nつなみひなんばしょ\r\n津波避難場所\r\nふくしひなんじょ\r\n福祉避難所\r\nいりょうかんけいきかん\r\n医療関係機関\r\nようはいりょしゃりようしせつ\r\n要配慮者利用施設\r\nしょうぼうしょ・しょうぼうだん\r\n消防署・消防団\r\nすいいかんそくじょ\r\n水位観測所\r\nはいすいぽんぷじょう\r\n排水ポンプ場\r\nきょう りょう 橋\r\nSign\r\nはんれい\r\n凡例 英語\r\nDesignated Emergency \r\nEvacuation Area\r\nDesignated Evacuation \r\nShelter (Center)\r\nFire Station ・\r\nWelfare Evacuation\r\nShelter (Center)\r\nTsunami Evacuation\r\nArea\r\nTsunami Evacuation\r\nBuilding\r\nMedical Related \r\nInstitution\r\nFacility for Those Who \r\nNeed Special Assistance\r\nVolunteer Fire Corps\r\nWater Level \r\nObservation Site\r\nDrain Pump Station\r\nBridge\r\nArea with Past Occurrence \r\nof Inundation inside a Levee\r\nInundation by River Water Inundation inside a levee\r\nYui River Inundation Damage Area（Estimated Large Scale)\r\nSource\r\nThis hazard map shows simultaneously the estimated high risk of flood inundation damage areas and the \r\nmaximum inundation depth when 3 rivers, Oi River, Yui River and Saguchiya River, overflow and the dikes are \r\nbroken due to estimated large-scale heavy rainfall (which possibly occurs once every 1000 years)."
      }
