    {
      "type": "heavy_rain",
      "areas": [
        "Oi River"
      ],
      "notes_ja": "Oi River の 1000 年に一度の大規模な大雨は 787mm/2days に達すると予測されている。これは過去最大の大雨 (509mm/2days)（1982 年台風 10 号）の約 1.5 倍である。",
      "source_page": 8,
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 8,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "Information about \r\nLegend\r\nAn estimated areas at risk of \r\nflood that might distroy \r\nhouses or bulidings\r\nArea at risk of \r\nriver bank erosion\r\nSediment disaster \r\nspecial hazard zone\r\nArea at risk of river \r\noverflow flooding\r\nSedimet disaster \r\nhazard zone\r\nInformation about \r\nsediment disaster\r\nInundation depth \r\n(Maximun expected scale)\r\n10.0m～less than 20.0m\r\n5.0m～less than 10.0m\r\n3.0m～less than 5.0m\r\n0.5m～less than 3.0m\r\n0～less than 0.5m\r\nA predicated large-scale heavy rainfall \r\n( that occurs once every 1000 years) of \r\nOi River, is expected to reach \r\n787mm/2days which is approximately 1.5 \r\ntimes of that the large rainfall ever \r\nrecorded (509mm/ 2days)(Typoon No 10 \r\nof 1982)."
      }
    },
