  "routes": [
    {
      "text_ja": "特別な事情がない限り、避難に車を使わない。消防車や緊急車両の活動に影響するため。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 4,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "Please do not use car when evacuating, \r\nbecause that would affect fire engines and \r\nother emergency vehicles activities, unless \r\nthere are special circumstances."
      }
    },
    {
      "text_ja": "避難所までの経路を事前に自分で決め、実際に安全に行けるか確認する。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 4,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "③ ④\r\n➀ ②\r\n \r\n⑦ ⑧\r\n⑤ ⑥ \r\n4\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\n●\r\nEvacuee life\r\nAcquire Knowledge on evacuation\r\nWhen stay safe at home or acquaintance's home When stay at evacuation shelter\r\n【 Precaution when entering an evacuation Sheltter 】\r\nDecide routes to evacuation shelter on your \r\nown in advance, and confirm the routes \r\nwhether can be reached safely to shelter or \r\nnot actually."
      }
    }
  ],
  "cautions": [
    {
      "text_ja": "家屋倒壊等氾濫想定区域：この区域に住む人、または家の高さが想定浸水深（水位）より低い人は、早めの避難を検討する。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 8,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "Houses collapse risk area: Resident lives \r\nin this area or the heighth of their house \r\nis lower than the estimated inundation \r\ndepth (water level) , please consider an \r\nearly evacuation\r\n➀\r\n② Houses \r\ncollapse\r\n大\r\n井\r\n川\r\nWeb-based Flood Simulation Serach System \r\nat an Arbitrary Point management by MLIT."
      }
    },
    {
      "text_ja": "外出すると命に危険がある場合は、その時点で今いる場所（自宅、建物など）の中で最も安全な場所へ避難する。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 7,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "In situations when going out would put your\r\n life at risk, evacuate to a safest place of your\r\n present location (home, building etc.) at the\r\n point of time to secure safety."
      }
    },
    {
      "text_ja": "高齢者、子ども、障害のある人などは早めに避難する。近所の支援が必要な人の避難を手助けする。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 4,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "Confirm the safe evacuation routes \r\nThe elderly, children and dissbiled person etc. \r\nin need of special assistance should make an \r\nearly evacuation. Please help nearby elderly, \r\ndisabled people etc. requiring special \r\nassistance (need, care) to evacuate."
      }
    },
    {
      "text_ja": "津波は繰り返し襲ってくる。必ずしも第一波が最大とは限らない。少なくとも12時間以上は警戒が必要",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/tsunami_hm_map.pdf",
        "page": 1,
        "method": "vision",
        "cited_text": null
      }
    },
    {
      "text_ja": "土砂災害が起きる前に前兆が現れる。前兆に気づいたら、できるだけ早く安全な場所へ避難する必要がある。",
      "source": {
        "file": "yoshida/kozui_hm_en.pdf",
        "page": 8,
        "method": "citation",
        "cited_text": "The warning signs will be appeared before sediment disaster occurs. When \r\nyou are conscious of the warning signs, you need to evacuate to a safty \r\nplace as sooner as possible."
      }
    }
  ],
